course: dictionary
lesson: 3583
title: Materials: what is fibreglass?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists and designers choose materials for their properties, which means what they are like. Fibreglass is light and strong, so it is good for things that must be strong without being heavy. «A cast is a hard shell of plaster or fibreglass shaped round a broken arm so that the bone cannot move while it heals.» Here the strength of the material keeps the arm still.
explain: Fibreglass is made of very thin glass threads, often set in plastic. The plastic holds the threads together, so they work as one strong material. Think of how a pile of loose threads is weak, but the same threads woven or set together can hold a load.
explain: Look at the word «fibreglass» in the cast sentence. The writer names it next to plaster, so you can tell both are materials used to make a hard shell. When you meet a new material, ask what it is made of and what job it does.
fact: Fibreglass is a light, strong material made of very thin glass threads, often set in plastic.
fact: Fibreglass is used to make boats, car bodies, helmets, slides and surfboards.
fact: Fibreglass is also used as insulation in lofts, to keep houses warm.
fact: Safety: fibreglass insulation can make your skin itch, so wear gloves when you handle it.
fact: Phrases you may see: a fibreglass boat, fibreglass insulation. Fibreglass is uncountable, so say some fibreglass, not a fibreglass.
exercise: What is fibreglass made of? | Thick blocks of wood | Soft wool from sheep | *Very thin glass threads, often set in plastic
exercise: Name one thing fibreglass is used to make. | A loaf of bread | *A surfboard | A pencil made of graphite
exercise: «A cast is a hard shell of plaster or fibreglass.» What job does the cast do? | It makes the bone grow faster | It keeps the broken arm wet | *It stops the broken bone moving while it heals | It makes the arm look smaller
test: Why is fibreglass a good material for making a boat? | *Because it is light and strong | Because it dissolves in water | Because it is soft and easy to bend by hand
test: Which safety tip is correct when you handle fibreglass insulation? | Rub it on your skin to test it | *Wear gloves, because it can make your skin itch | Hold it close to a fire to check it
exam: Which word from the cast sentence names a material made of thin glass threads? | *Fibreglass | Heals | Cast | Bone
